<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable CURSOR CONNECTOR layer — Windows peer of
    AgentLens/Services/CursorConnector/*.swift (the log-stream manager, connector
    models, session state machine, and the secret broker). Portable-first so every
    seam is provable via `dotnet test` on the macOS authoring host; the runtime
    halves that actually spawn the proxy/cloudflared process, open a TCP secret
    broker listener, tail a live file, or read/write the on-disk state.vscdb belong
    in the deferred OpenBurnBar.App.CursorConnector.Windows sibling (bucket B).

    Faithful parity map (Swift oracle → this project):
      • ConnectorModels.cs                — CursorConnectorModels.swift
      • ConnectorProviderCatalog.cs       — ConnectorProvider metadata + Cursor-
                                            Manager.supportedModel/provider(forBaseURL)
      • CursorConnectorLogStreamManager.cs— CursorConnectorLogStreamManager.swift
      • UsageEventNormalizer.cs           — CursorConnectorManager.normalizeUsageEvent
      • UsageLogConsumer.cs               — CursorConnectorManager.consumeUsageLogChunk
      • TryCloudflareUrlExtractor.cs      — CursorConnectorManager.extractTryCloudflareURL
      • CursorConnectorSecretBroker.cs    — CursorConnectorManager+SecretBroker.swift
      • RoutedClientConfigSyncService.cs  — RoutedClientConfigSyncService (models)
      • CursorSettingsApplier.cs          — backupAndApplyCursorSettings/restore
      • CursorConnectorSession.cs         — connect()/disconnect() state machine
      • Seams.cs                          — KeychainStore/FileHandle/SecRandom/Date seams

    State.vscdb reads are COMPOSED with the landed CursorStateDbReader
    (app/OpenBurnBar.App.Quota.Acquisition) — never duplicated. Referencing that
    project also gives the connector the same Microsoft.Data.Sqlite stack for the
    deferred .Windows ItemTable read/write half.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.App.CursorConnector</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.App.CursorConnector</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Compose with the landed state.vscdb reader (CursorStateDbReader /
         CursorStateCredentials); the connector reuses it for Cursor account
         identity rather than opening its own ItemTable reader. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\OpenBurnBar.App.Quota.Acquisition\OpenBurnBar.App.Quota.Acquisition.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
